      "side": 1,
      "message": "Making use of mid-stack inlining is a good idea, I hadn\u0027t thought of that. Definitely not worth compromising the API for performance.\n\nI think running the chacha20poly1305 benchmarks with GOARCH\u003d386 and the -benchmem flag would be the easiest way to check the allocation numbers. So long as they don\u0027t go up we should be fine. Checking other architectures as well wouldn\u0027t hurt though. I\u0027m going to do some work on chacha20poly1305 (to port poly1305.MAC to s390x) this cycle anyway so I\u0027ll do some extra performance testing on s390x then.\n\nYeah Uint32 has a high inlining cost which is a pain. Historically we\u0027ve resisted making functions that the compiler can optimize intrinsics since it would be better to improve the inlining heuristics but maybe we should just do it. Even with Uint32 being an intrinsic though it still might not inline, so the mid-stack approach you suggested is probably best.",
